        <definition>enum AVPixelFormat AVHWFramesContext::sw_format</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>sw_format</name>
        <qualifiedname>AVHWFramesContext::sw_format</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The pixel format identifying the actual data layout of the hardware frames. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Must be set by the caller before calling <ref refid="hwcontext_8h_1a66a7e1ebc7e459ce07d3de6639ac7e38" kindref="member">av_hwframe_ctx_init()</ref>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>when the underlying API does not provide the exact data layout, but only the colorspace/bit depth, this field should be set to the fully planar version of that format (e.g. for 8-bit 420 YUV it should be AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P, not AV_PIX_FMT_NV12 or anything else). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
